# If this vault is edited from more than one machine, git's core.autocrlf rewrites line
# endings per machine, and files show as "modified" when their content is identical. Two
# real consequences:
#   1. Phantom conflicts when two machines push the same untouched file.
#   2. A Stop hook that refuses to end a session with uncommitted notes blocks on a vault
#      that only LOOKS dirty - a session that cannot end until someone commits nothing.
# So normalise everything to LF in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
